# Read by `trivy` directly (aquasecurity/trivy-action passes this path via
# the `trivyignores` input on the image-scan step in .github/workflows/build.yml).
#
# CVE-2026-34040 / GO-2026-4887 — Moby AuthZ plugin bypass on oversized
# request bodies. Daemon-side flaw in the authorization-plugin path; this
# image only ever runs the runner binary, which is an API *client*
# (internal/docker) and never serves or validates plugin requests. Fixed
# upstream only under the github.com/moby/moby/v2 module path (v2.0.0-beta.8),
# which is still a beta and a breaking import-path migration — no released
# version of github.com/docker/docker carries the fix, so no dependency bump
# clears this. Same advisory, same reasoning, as the ALLOWLIST entry in
# scripts/check-runner-vulns.mjs (the govulncheck gate). Remove this line
# once github.com/docker/docker itself ships a fixed release.
CVE-2026-34040

# ── dind-only: stale Go toolchain baked into docker:29.7.2-dind's pre-built
# binaries (dockerd, containerd, containerd-shim-runc-v2, ctr, runc, docker,
# docker-proxy) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This repo does not compile any of these; they ship as-is inside the docker
# base image (Dockerfile `dind` stage), and 29.7.2 is upstream's latest
# published `-dind` tag — there is no newer release to bump to. Every entry
# below is a Go stdlib/x/net/x/text/x/mod/grpc-go advisory reachable only if
# something feeds these binaries attacker-controlled network input, and this
# variant's dockerd never gets one: docker-compose.dind.yml documents no host
# port bind for it, DOCKER_TLS_CERTDIR is forced empty, and
# dind-entrypoint.sh starts dockerd with an explicit unix:// --host so it
# never opens the TCP/TLS listener these HTTP/2, DNS-message and TLS advisories
# target. containerd's gRPC socket (the xDS/RBAC advisory) is the same story:
# local unix socket for internal engine IPC, never exposed. Reviewed
# 2026-08-20. Re-review if this variant ever grows a network-facing listener,
# and drop entries individually as docker:*-dind picks up a Go toolchain that
# clears them.
CVE-2026-25681
CVE-2026-27136
CVE-2026-33814
